WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.390
To be the master of space.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:08.470
But you can only master a place that you already know.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.320
One could spend their life
in comfort in such a place.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.450
But others choose to seek new worlds in unknown space.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.360
This is fate.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.160
Which path will Kato Marika, pirate and high school girl, choose?

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.360
I had no idea Luca was replaced by an android.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.590
Normally, you barely knew she was there at all.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.340
Yeah, didn't think that would work.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.550
Reformat

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:42.520
The main computer was still functional,
but when she shut down it reformatted itself.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.650
I couldn't get any clues as to whose android it was.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.580
What was the make and model?

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.370
It's a one-off made by a Galactic Empire corporation called Human Torch.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:56.530
Probably for a Stellar Military special operation.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.120
How was she transmitting our information?

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.870
Um,

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.420
what do you think happened to the real Luca?

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.230
She's a pirate.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:11.190
She always knew this could happen.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.880
A strange woman, but I'll miss her.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:17.470
Hi.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.430
L... L...

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.410
Lu-Lu-Lu-Lu-Lu...

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.780
How rude.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.900
You can see I have legs.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:14.020
So you changed vacation plans, and ended up at a different resort planet?

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:14.590
Yes.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.130
Initially, I planned to watch an aurora there.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.340
But we saw plenty during that yacht race.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.060
So I went to a warm planet.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.310
No one attacked you?

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.100
Or kidnapped you?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.270
Lots of men invited me places.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.310
Everywhere I went.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.110
I rather enjoyed it.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.250
Then you're really giving all these to me?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:51.960
Sure.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.210
I've had my fun already.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.180
I must thank you.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.890
Yeah, I'll pass that along.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.870
I'm glad I got to see the legendary Blaster in action.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.250
How fortunate for you.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.630
Blaster?

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.630
Unfortunately, we can't find that intruder.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.890
We'll need to double our guards.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:50.220
She claimed to be captain of the Grand Cross?

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.850
Yeah, that's what she said.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.140
Could she have been lying?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:57.650
Why would an enemy captain come here alone?

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.860
I don't know.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:03.150
But she had the same feel about her...

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.530
As what?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.070
She felt like a pirate.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:10.490
Captain!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:11.330
Trouble!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.080
What's wrong?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.790
A weird woman in the conference room!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.730
What?

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.820
Another ship is docking: the Parabellum.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.570
Oh, that's fine.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:46.530
Leave them.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.450
I thought they'd make an appearance.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.940
A cape and a skull...

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.780
Be seated, pirates!

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:31.530
This is the pirate's nest: A place for pirates that only pirates may enter!

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.580
Put your guns away.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.410
No killing is allowed here.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.870
What about her?!

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:43.500
The only girl who's become a pirate recently
is the Bentenmaru's captain over there!

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:47.550
Hi.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.100
I can understand why a young man like you wouldn't know this.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.310
What?

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:59.440
I imagine most here don't know, so I'll tell you.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.730
I'm surprised.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.610
She really did come.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.690
Dad?

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:11.740
There are more pirates than just those with Letters of Marque.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.450
Observe the skull on her shoulder.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:19.660
It signifies a space pirate recognized
and endorsed by the Galactic Empire!

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:28.260
A legendary pirate?

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.970
When I was a kid, I thought it was a fairy tale.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:42.190
The idea for the Letters of Marque was stolen from the pirates of the Galactic Empire!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.440
Stolen?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.940
When you're desperate, you'll try anything.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:53.200
We help the independent governments, and we profit from it.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.540
Well, that was what made me become a pirate, anyway.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.160
Got that right.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.750
Uh, you all are...

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:07.170
We are the original...
One... Two...

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:08.750
How many again?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.380
I'm Ten.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.340
You're Eight.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.850
I'm Nine.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:21.980
You might say we're a step down from the Original Seven.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.570
The three of us were up drinking all night.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:30.360
So they reached the government office before us.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.360
That's right.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.080
I am Quartz Christie!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.450
One of the imperial pioneers who journeys through unknown space.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:45.370
And what is a pioneer like that doing here?

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:50.840
This is a frontier system, where even the
Empire's seventh fleet never ventures.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:54.800
There's no reason for you to come here.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.890
I'd guess you've heard it from Kato Marika.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.690
Right now, I pilot the Mobile Battleship Grand Cross.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.650
My goal is to hunt pirates.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.820
Let's fight.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.910
She's underestimating us.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.700
That's why she's here.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.160
That's all the more reason!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.790
No killing is permitted in the pirate's nest!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.210
Right?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:35.880
That's correct.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.590
Let's have a fair fight.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.350
It's much better for you than sending spies and laying ambushes.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.650
Isn't that why you came?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.240
I'll win.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:54.820
Are you sure of this?

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.610
That's my line.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:00.320
In other words, it's a good deal for both of us.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.390
I refuse to accept that!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.010
Why must we have a fair fight?

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.800
And you call yourselves pirates?

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.270
I'm going to kill her right here.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.140
That'll end this.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.190
I see.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.200
I thought it looked familiar.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.660
Quartz, I'm here to get you!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:44.930
Shut up!

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.580
Who are you?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.710
I am Ironbeard.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.290
I hail from a faraway sea.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.880
You're with her?

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:03.220
At the Queen's request, Quartz Christie,

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:06.100
I have come to retrieve you.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:08.520
I see.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.020
It's been a long time, chef.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.690
Yes, I've been waiting.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.610
Want to eat before you go?

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.990
It's the special menu today!

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.030
No, I'll pass.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.950
I've come to fetch this tomboy.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.950
Hey, wait a second.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:28.450
Ahem...

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.960
Who the heck are you?!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.680
I can understand Quartz.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:50.060
For whatever reason, she doesn't seem to like us.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.890
So, you want to destroy the pirates?

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.650
Then bring it on.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.270
But what about you?

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.400
Marika...

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.700
Are you our enemy? Or a friend?

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.410
The end of space.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:12.620
One man who can see into the endless future isn't enough.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:19.130
Only when others stand with him will we someday see the end of space.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:27.300
Captain of the Bentenmaru, Kato Marika, what is it you see?

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.310
Is Marika having that conference now?

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:39.320
Gruier said that they reached the pirate's nest.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:44.150
I'm sure she's going crazy in front of the guys.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.490
Crazy!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.030
What do you mean by "crazy"?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:51.790
Well, regardless, we have to hold down the fort while she's gone.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:52.580
Yup.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.540
That's right.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.130
I hope it goes well.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.220
This is pirate heaven.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.130
Yell at one another, and talk with one another.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.100
But don't spill the food! Don't spit it out!

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.810
In the vastness of space, food is a treasure!

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:20.190
Food is a treasure! Food is a treasure! Food is a treasure!

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.480
Now, let's begin.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:28.450
But one of us disappeared during all that.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.280
What should we do?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:30.950
Leave them.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.410
It could be a good lesson for the kid.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.080
He needs to learn a hard lesson.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.840
A pirate coming to meet a pirate?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.130
I'm amazed you'd accept the job.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:45.180
It's a job from the Queen.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:50.010
I planned to get the drop on them,
and Kato Marika ended up running the show.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.470
And then you hogged the spotlight.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.640
I've been humiliated.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:57.480
Your safety is more important than your dignity.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:03.730
Kato Marika was doing something similar,
guarding a pirate named Stone.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:04.780
Captain...

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.710
As anticipated.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.960
Pirates in the frontier systems are cowards.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.080
What are you going to do?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.880
You know what.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.910
I don't care about the Queen or the Empire.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:26.220
If I kill you, I'll be safe.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.550
You really think so?

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.220
Of course!

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.940
Captain!

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.280
Don't move, kids!

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:50.660
Jeez...

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.740
So he came to meet her,
and you came to meet them?

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.200
Thank you.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:55.740
How about it?

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.040
You could officially join my crew.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.660
You're serious?

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.790
This is a special freebie.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.550
No killing.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.860
Sorry, they found me out.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:13.510
I see.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:18.140
Ironbeard, it appears you've been handling our Kane.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.270
Thank you.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.520
Hey, Misa.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.610
Don't "hey" me!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.480
What are you doing out here?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:26.650
What?

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.190
A new job.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.110
Did you tell Marika?

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.570
I told her I was getting a new job.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:34.620
She's very supportive.

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:35.830
Honestly...

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.500
Anyway, older brother over there?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.790
Younger brother.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:46.460
Kane, I'm subtracting the days
your brother worked from your salary.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:54.090
And your younger brother will pay a penalty for all the days he was on the Bentenmaru without permission.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.510
I'll send the bill to the Parabellum.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.270
So, what did you want to learn?

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:06.060
What was so important that you
needed twin helmsmen to learn?

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:13.240
The pirates in this area are about to be given a choice:

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:20.620
To become true pirates, or to cling to their Letters of Marque and remain pirates for hire.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:25.040
I liked the look in her eyes.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.500
I have seen how the flow will change.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.960
To see such a sparkle in someone's eyes

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:35.390
here in the frontier systems was truly an honor!

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.980
It can't be easy for your daughter,
having a parent put so much on her.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.440
She chose this path.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.690
But I didn't expect this much from her.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.910
The Parabellum has left port.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.450
Got it!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.160
Looks good.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.160
Pirate's
Council
After-
Party

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:14.760
A sweet sauce combining honey and spices from all over the Galactic Empire, aged for 500 years.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:21.090
This is the greatest dessert of my father, the man who
brought together the members of the first Pirate's Council!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.020
You're not listening!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:27.520
The ultimate taste, a sweetness that melts the rough heart of a pirate.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.900
How many years has it been?

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:35.280
Well, it's been since the last council...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.910
When was the last council?

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:38.990
I forget!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.830
So, Captain Marika...

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:44.250
Yes?

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:49.000
We can decide the exact time later,
but who will take command?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:56.010
Command aside, the question is who will be the control point for the electronic warfare.

00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:59.140
Which means...

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.180
Hi.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:06.230
I'm Coorie, the Bentenmaru's electronic warfare specialist.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:10.230
I will be the control point for the
electronic warfare portion of this fight.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.900
Nice to meet you all.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:15.900
Um, it isn't that anyone here is
more important than the rest.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:20.950
It's just that the Bentenmaru is the only
one that's fought the Grand Cross.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.530
Keep that in mind.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.450
Bravo!

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.710
Let's do our best!

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.460
We're counting on you, Coorie!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.690
Coorie!

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:32.040
Oh, okay.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.000
Let's all do our best for Coorie!

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.430
It's so strange.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:47.850
I was sure those guys would prefer your outside clothes.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:52.060
An EW specialist spends most of the day confronting the truth.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.530
And? How's the Bentenmaru?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:57.440
Right, right.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:01.410
We've upped sensors and radars by about twenty percent.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:05.370
Engine output has also been upped, primarily by the thrusters,

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:09.330
so Kane will be able to do some pretty crazy stunts.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.500
Crazy? Like what?

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.090
It's something for you to look forward to.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.420
Hey, it's the crazy.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:18.470
What's up?

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:24.970
I was just thinking that if the other pirates knew

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:28.810
we picked the date based around your final exams, what would they say?

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:33.110
I should tell them after it's over.

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.820
It'll make for a funny story.

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.400
No, no, no, no.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.570
That can be the Bentenmaru's secret.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:43.200
Hey, isn't it about time for the transmission to start?

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.490
Not looking forward to that, either.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:52.960
This will be something to see.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.250
<b>Space Mandarin Oranges
Or maybe something to hear?</b>

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:04.890
<i>Give a shout! A battle cry!</i>

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:10.020
<i>We don't take anyone's help,</i>

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.240
<i>but if we don't like you, we'll gang up and beat you up.</i>

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:13.310
I love it.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.400
We know the time and the place.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:18.190
<i>The drink when we're done is delicious.
Turn it up, and let it play through the ship!</i>

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:19.650
Right!

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:20.320
<i>The drink when we're done is delicious.</i>

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:24.820
<i>The men and women. The pirates are strong!</i>

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:27.530
Dad... I'll kill you!
<i>Drinking and fighting. A pirate's soul!</i>

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.540
<i>Drinking and fighting. A pirate's soul!</i>

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:34.000
<i>Give a shout! A battle cry!</i>

